{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/optics/refraction/","source":"students/subjects/physics/optics/refraction.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Refraction & Snell's Law | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/optics/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Optics</a></nav>\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Refraction &amp; Snell's Law</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Snell's law: n1 sinθ1 = n2 sinθ2. Refractive index relates wave speed in media: n = c/v.</p>\n      <section class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Practice</h2>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n          <li>Light goes from air (n≈1.00) into glass (n≈1.5) with incident angle 30°. Find refracted angle.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Solution</h2>\n        <p>sinθ2 = n1/n2 sinθ1 = (1/1.5) × 0.5 = 0.333 → θ2 ≈ 19.47°.</p>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif} .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(16px);backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}